      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-184825",
      ":question/problem": "Prove by contradiction that $10x + 35y \\ne 2$ for any $x, y \u2208 Z$.\n\nAssume, for a contradiction, that\n{{field-1}} $x, y \u2208$\n{{field-2}}\n{{field-3}}\n{{field-4}}.\n\nFactoring the expression on the left-hand side gives\n$5(2x + 7y) \\le 2$ {{field-5}}\n\nLet $a =$ {{field-6}}. Since $x$ and $y$ are {{field-7}}, we have that $a$ is {{field-8}}.\n\nHence, we have {{field-9}}, which means {{field-10}}. But this is a contradiction since {{field-11}}."
